#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:3
msgid "Dependency cooldown"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:5
msgid ""
"Skip index artifacts uploaded in the last few days, so maintainers have time "
"to catch and yank a compromised or broken release before your machine picks "
"it up. Reach for this when you install or upgrade tools from a public index "
"and can afford to lag the newest version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:11
msgid "Set it per command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:13
msgid ""
"``--cooldown DAYS`` works on ``install``, ``install-all``, ``inject``, "
"``upgrade``, ``upgrade-all`` and ``run``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:15
msgid "$ pipx install --cooldown 7 httpie"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:19
msgid ""
"pipx translates one policy for both backends: `pip <https://pip.pypa.io/>`__ "
"receives ``--uploaded-prior-to P7D`` and `uv <https://github.com/astral-sh/"
"uv>`__ receives ``--exclude-newer P7D``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:22
msgid ""
"Under the pip backend the cooldown also covers the shared pip that pipx "
"installs or refreshes during the command. A new shared environment starts "
"from the oldest pip pipx supports, then upgrades only to a release older "
"than the cooldown; when none is, or the index publishes no upload times, "
"pipx keeps that oldest pip. The metadata value in the table below does not "
"apply here: only ``--cooldown`` and ``PIPX_COOLDOWN`` do, and ``pipx upgrade-"
"shared`` ignores both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:29
msgid "Set it for a machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:31
msgid "Export ``PIPX_COOLDOWN`` so every one of those commands picks it up:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:33
msgid ""
"$ export PIPX_COOLDOWN=7\n"
"$ pipx install httpie\n"
"$ pipx upgrade-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:39
msgid ""
"Put the export in your shell profile to make it stick across sessions. pipx "
"has no configuration file; see :doc:`Environment variables <../reference/"
"environment-variables>` for the full list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:44
msgid "Which value pipx uses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:50
msgid "Rank"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:51
msgid "Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:52
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:53
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:54
msgid "``--cooldown DAYS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:55
msgid ""
"Wins over everything. ``--cooldown 0`` opts one command out of a machine-"
"wide setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:56
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:57
msgid "``PIPX_COOLDOWN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:58
msgid ""
"Applies to the commands listed above. Outranks whatever an earlier install "
"recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:59
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:60
msgid "``cooldown_days`` in the environment's metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:61
msgid ""
"The value the environment's last install recorded. See :doc:`Metadata <../"
"reference/metadata>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:63
msgid ""
"A locked install ignores all three: ``pylock.toml`` already pins every "
"version. Passing ``--cooldown`` together with ``--lock`` errors, while "
"``PIPX_COOLDOWN`` yields and the install proceeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:68
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:70
msgid "Read back the variable and the value the environment recorded:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:72
msgid ""
"$ pipx environment --value PIPX_COOLDOWN\n"
"7\n"
"$ pipx list --output json | jq "
"'.venvs.httpie.metadata.main_package.cooldown_days'\n"
"7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:79
msgid "An invalid value stops the command before it starts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/dependency-cooldown.rst:81
msgid ""
"$ PIPX_COOLDOWN=lots pipx install httpie\n"
"PIPX_COOLDOWN must be unset or a non-negative integer, got 'lots'."
msgstr ""
